<p>The way I view this is that looking at the object constitutes a measurement: a collection of apparent dimensions and light wavelengths. So it's interesting that the object seems to have a consistent appearance. For all we know, it's actually something completely different &#8212; possibly even something that constantly changes form &#8212; and the errors are a side-effect of its 'perception filter'.</p>
<p>Or maybe I'm overthinking it and the object is simply immune to itself. Never know with reality warpers ; )</p>

